; worldswap.eval — a world is loaded when a game starts, and switched in the
; process (docs/world-on-demand.md). WorldTest reads the `worlds status` lines.
;
; The FIRST status is taken before any game has started: the title screen must
; have no world at all. Then A -> B -> A, with a status after each, so the SRV
; count after coming back to A can be compared with the first visit's — a
; switch that leaks textures (or anything else holding a descriptor slot)
; shows up there, not in whether the switch "worked".
;
; wt_swap is made from the title screen, where no world is loaded: its catalogs
; come from the default world (CreateWorld's template). WorldTest removes it.
logecho on
worlds status
worlds new wt_swap
reset
worlds status
worlds load wt_swap
worlds status
worlds load dungeon-demo
worlds status
worlds load dungeon-demo
worlds status
